<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14192" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dis-cŏŏpĕrĭo</span></b> ,
			pĕrui, pertum, 4, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to uncover, disclose, lay
				bare, expose</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Lev. 21, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turpitudinem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 18, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verecundiora patris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Ezech. 22, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to put off, take
				off, remove</i> a covering: pallium, id. Ruth, 3,
			4.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to expose,
			disclose</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">peccata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Thren. 4, 22</span></i>
			.</div>
